# .assetsignore — Cloudflare Pages never serves these, even if the project's output directory is
# the repo root. This is the SECOND line of defence: the first is that the host publishes dist/
# (see tools/build_site.sh and tools/server-shift-plan.md §7b), which simply does not contain them.
#
# Keep this list in sync with the "forbidden" list in tools/tests/publish_sim.js — that test fails
# if a dev file ever reaches the publish directory on either path.
#
# The game fetches exactly three things at runtime: /index.html, /assets/**, /Updates/Sprite/**,
# so everything else in this repo is safe to exclude. Note the entries are explicit and contain no
# `!` re-includes: if this file were ever the only protection, nothing the game needs disappears.

# --- dev material -------------------------------------------------------------
tools/
Sprite/
image-search/

# --- Updates/ : only Sprite/ ships (the animated class PNGs) -------------------
Updates/ApngAnimation/
Updates/cards-gear-audit/
Updates/map-sprites-v2/
Updates/retired-v1-kit/
Updates/v27-organic-field/
Updates/Sprite/index.html
Updates/maps sprite.html
Updates/ro_atlas.js

# --- legacy pages, harnesses and screenshots ----------------------------------
_login.html
_shot.html
logic2.js
_recon_v27b.png
_recon_v27c.png
_recon_v27d.png
_recon_v27e.png

# --- repo documents (nothing here is read by the browser) ---------------------
AGENTS.md
READ-ME-FIRST.md
.gitignore
